+**The module that applies the plugin is the one whose build types choose.** Put
+the plugin in the module whose code uses the client, and declare in THAT module
+every build type that should compile its own environment. If the client lives in
+a library (say `:data`) and the app has a build type the library does not declare
+(`featureX` with `matchingFallbacks += listOf("debug")`), AGP packs the library's
+`debug` build into the `featureX` APK — and with it `debug`'s environment. The
+library has no `featureX` variant, so no rule above can pick `featureX` there.
+The plugin says so: a warning at configuration and, on every generation of the
+fallback, `` Palbase: debug → main (…) — ALSO packed into `:app` featureX … ``. Fix
+it by declaring the build type in the library too
+(`create("featureX") { initWith(getByName("debug")) }`), or state that the
+fallback's stack is intended: `palbase.env.featureX=main`. (This check reads the
+app module's build types, so it is skipped under Isolated Projects.) Applying the
+plugin to BOTH the app and a library generates `io.palbase.generated` twice and
+is not a supported layout.
+
